/RESTORE LINCTAPE BY ZACHARY KIRTZ
/THIS PROGRAM WILL RESTORE (WRITE) A LINCTAPE DUMP
/READ OVER SERIAL TO A LINCTAPE MOUNTED ON UNIT 0

/REQUIREMENTS:
/1. A PDP-12 WITH A FUNCTIONING TC12
/2. AT LEAST ONE FUNCTION TU55/TU56 TAPE TRANSPORT
/3. A KL8E SERIAL CARD EQUIVALENT
/4. AT LEAST 4K OF CORE MEMORY
/5. ANOTHER SYSTEM CAPABLE OF RUNNING THE REST_LINC
/   (OR EQUIV) PROGRAM WITH A SERIAL CONNECTION TO THE
/   PDP-12'S KL8E EQUIVALENT CARD

/TO USE THIS PROGRAM:
/1. LOAD THIS PROGRAM USING THE STANDARD BIN LOADER
/2. SET THE MODE SWITCH TO "8"
/3. PRESS "I/O PRESET"
/4. MOUNT A LINCTAPE ON A TU55 OR TU56 TRANSPORT
/   SET TO UNIT NUMBER 0 (OR 8).
/5. SET "WRITE ENABLE" AND "REMOTE" ON THE TRANSPORT
/   THE TAPE HAS BEEN MOUNTED ON.
/6. START REST_LINC ON THE OTHER SYSTEM
/7. START FROM EITHER ADDRESS 20 (USING "START 20")
/   OR ADDRESS 200.
/8. THIS PROGRAM WILL BEGIN RECEIVING BLOCKS FROM
/   REST_LINC AND WRITING THEM TO THE MOUNTED TAPE.
/9. ONCE FINISHED, THIS PROGRAM WILL SPOOL THE
/   MOUNTED TAPE BACK TO BLOCK ZERO THEN HALT
/   AT ADDRESS 177.
/   AT THIS POINT, THIS PROGRAM CAN BE RUN AGAIN BY
/   PRESSING THE CONTINUE SWITCH.

/MEMORY REQUIREMENTS
/	THIS PROGRAM ONLY REQUIRES 4K OF MEMORY.
/	THE FIRST 1000 (OCTAL) WORDS ARE OCCUPIED BY
/	THE PROGRAM ITSELF.
/	LOCATIONS 1000 TO 7600 ARE USED AS A BUFFER FOR
/	RECEIVING TAPE BLOCK DATA.
/	LOCATIONS 7600 TO 7777, WHICH ARE OCCUPIED BY
/	OS/8, THE RIMLOAD, AND THE BINLOADER,
/	ARE UNTOUCHED.

/CONTROLS
/SR0 -	ABORT WRITING TO THE TAPE
/	THIS WILL IMMEDIATELY CEASE WRITING TO THE 
/	TAPE, SPOOL THE TAPE BACK TO BLOCK 0, AND HALT
/	THIS PROGRAM AT ADDRESS 177.
/	THIS PROGRAM CAN BE RUN AGAIN BY PRESSING
/	THE CONTINUE SWITCH. THIS WILL START
/	WRITING BACK AT BLOCK ZERO; PREVIOUS
/	PROGRESS IS LOST.
/SR1 -	SKIP CURRENT TAPE OPERATION
/	THIS WILL SKIP THE TAPE OPERATION CURRENTLY
/	BEING PERFORMED.
/	THE INTENDED USE FOR THIS IS TO SKIP OVER
/	BLOCKS THAT CANNOT BE SEEKED TO (I.E., UNIT
/	SHOESHINES FOREVER WHILE TRYING TO SEEK).
/	THIS IS ACCOMPLISHED BY FORCING AN I/O
/	PRESET.
/	AFTER PRESSING SR1, IT MUST BE RELEASED
/	FOR THE PROGRAM TO CONTINUE.

/ON THE PDP-12, THERE ARE THREE DIFFERENT TAPE FORMATS
/THAT ARE TYPICALLY USED:
/512 BLOCKS,  256 WORDS - LINC FORMAT (LAP6-DIAL)
/896 BLOCKS,  256 WORDS - EXT LINC FORMAT (LAP6-DIAL)
/1536 BLOCKS, 129 WORDS - TYPICALLY USED BY OS/8
/
/THIS PROGRAM SUPPORTS RESTORING TO TAPES USING
/THREE FORMATS.
/IT ALSO SUPPORTS RESTORING TO TAPES USING OTHER
/FORMATS, SO LONG AS THEY USE A CONSISTENT BLOCK SIZE
/(I.E., ALL BLOCKS ARE OF SIZE N)

/THIS PROGRAM SENDS AND RECEIVES DATA OVER SERIAL
/USING THREE FORMATS:
/1 8-BIT BYTE CONTAINGING 1 8-BIT BYTE
/2 8-BIT BYTES CONTAINING 1 12-BIT WORD
/3 8-BIT BYTES CONTAINING 2 12-BIT WORDS
/
/THE 1 BYTE FORMAT IS USED FOR INFORMATION WHERE ONLY
/8 BITS OF INFORMATION ARE REQUIRED.
/IT IS MAINLY USED WHEN SENDING AND RECEIVING
/FLAGS AND COMMANDS
/
/THE TWO BYTE FORMAT PACKS A SINGLE 12-BIT WORD INTO
/TWO 8-BIT BYTES. THE FIRST BYTE CONTAINS THE BOTTOM
/8 BITS OF THE 12 BIT WORD (BITS 4 TO 11) AND THE
/SECOND BYTE CONTAINS THE TOP 4 BITS OF THE 12 BIT
/WORD (BITS 0 TO 3).
/THIS FORMAT IS USED FOR SENDING AND RECEIVING
/SIZE AND CHECKSUM INFORMATION, WHERE ONLY A SINGLE
/12-BIT WORD OF INFORMATION IS REQUIRED.
/IT IS ALSO USED TO RECEIVE THE FINAL WORD OF A
/BLOCK WHEN ODD-SIZED BLOCK FORMATS ARE BEING USED.
/
/THE THREE BYTE FORMAT PACKS TWO 12-BIT WORDS INTO
/THREE 8-BIT BYTES. THE FIRST BYTE CONTAINS THE
/BOTTOM 8 BITS OF THE FIRST WORD
/(BITS 4 TO 11). THE SECOND BYTE CONTAINS THE TOP
/4 BITS (BITS 0 TO 3) OF THE FIRST WORD IN ITS
/BOTTOM HALF (BITS 4 TO 7) AND THE BOTTOM 4 BITS
/(BITS 8 TO 11) OF THE SECOND WORD IN ITS TOP HALF
/(BITS 0 TO 3). THE THIRD BYTE CONTAINS THE TOP 8
/BITS (BITS 0 TO 7) OF THE SECOND WORD.
/THIS FORMAT IS USED FOR RECEIVING BLOCK DATA
/EXCEPT WHEN THE LAST WORD OF AN ODD-LENGTH BLOCK
/IS BEING READ, WHERE THE 2 BYTE FORMAT IS USED.

/THIS PROGRAM BEGINS BY READING THE FIRST BLOCK
/OF THE LINCTAPE MOUNTED ON UNIT 0.
/THE ADDRESS LEFT IN TMA IS USED TO DETERMINE THE
/BLOCK SIZE BEING USED BY THE TAPE.
/THIS CALCULATED BLOCK SIZE IS SENT TO THE OTHER
/SYSTEM USING THE TWO BYTE FORMAT.
/
/TO REQUEST A BLOCK, THIS PROGRAM WILL SEND 0XFF OVER
/SERIAL USING THE SINGLE BYTE FORMAT.
/IT WILL THEN WAIT FOR A SINGLE BYTE REPLY.
/
/IF IT RECEIVES 0XFF (SEND_BLOCK), IT WILL BEGIN\
/READING BLKLEN WORDS OF DATA OVER SERIAL USING THE TWO
/AND THREE BYTE FORMATS.
/ALL BLOCK DATA IS READ USING THE THREE BYTE
/FORMAT, EXCEPT FOR THE FINAL WORD WHEN ODD BLOCK
/LENGTH FORMATS ARE USED, WHERE THE TWO BYTE FORMAT
/IS USED.
/
/IF IT INSTEAD RECEIVES 0XFE (FINISH), IT WILL A FINISH
/FLAG THAT WILL BE CHECKED LATER.
/
/AFTER RECEIVING BLOCK DATA, THIS PROGRAM WILL PROCEED
/TO WRITE ALL RECEIVED BLOCKS, IF ANY, TO THE MOUNTED
/TAPE.
/
/AFTER WRITING ALL RECEIVED BLOCKS, THIS PROGRAM WILL
/USE THE LINCTAPE "CHK" INSTRUCTION TO QUICKLY CHECK
/FOR ERRORS IN ALL OF THE WRITTEN BLOCKS.
/THIS ONLY CHECKS THE WRITTEN BLOCKS USING A 12-BIT
/CHECKSUM AND ISN'T PERFECTLY RELIABLE, BUT WILL CATCH
/MOST ERRORS.
/
/FINALLY, THIS PROGRAM WILL CHECK IF THE FINISH FLAG
/HAS BEEN SET (I.E., BECAUSE IT RECEIVED THE FINISH
/FLAG WHEN RECEIVING BLOCKS EARLIER) AND, IF SET,
/RESET ITSELF AND SPOOL THE MOUNTED TAPE BACK TO
/BLOCK 0.
/SERIAL/KL8E IOTS
KSF2=6401		/SKIP ON FLAG SET
KRB2=6406		/BUF->AC

TSF2=6411		/SKIP ON FLAG SET
TLS2=6416		/AC->BUF

/PDP-12 INSTRUCTIONS
LINC=6141	/8-MODE:SWITCH TO LINC MODE
PDP= 0002	/L-MODE:SWITCH TO PDP8 MODE
TMA= 0023	/L-MODE:AC -> TMA SETUP
TAC= 0003	/L-MODE:TAPE AC -> AC
AXO= 0001	/L-MODE:AC -> TAPE XOB
ESF= 0004	/L-MODE:AC->SPECIAL FUNCTIONS
TMIR=6151	/8-MODE:LOAD TAPE MAINT REG
TMCP=6152	/8-MODE:GEN TC12 CONTROL PULSE
TMTR=6154	/8-MODE:COPY TC12 REG TO/FROM AC
DVI= 7407	/8-MODE:DIVIDE MQ BY C(PC)

/BUFFER SIZE
/PRESERVE OS/8 CORE RESIDENT LOCATIONS
BUFSZ=7600-BUF

*20
JMP I KENT		/JUMP TO ACTUAL ENTRY

/PAGE 0 VARIABLES
FNSHFG,	0	/FINISH FLAG
CHKSM,	0	/CHECKSUM
TRIES,	0	/RETRY COUNT
RCVBUF,	0	/RECEIVE BUFFER ADDR (FOR RECV3)
BLKIDX,	0	/CURRENT BLOCK NUMBER
BLKLEN,	0	/(1ST) BLOCK LENGTH
BUFCNT,	0	/NUM OF BLOCKS FIT IN BUF
BLKCNT,	0	/NUM OF BLOCKS IN BUF

/PAGE 0 CONSTANTS
KBFADR,	BUF	/BUFFER START OFFSET
KBUFSZ,	BUFSZ	/BUFFER SIZE
KTRYCT,	-10	/COM MAX RETRY COUNT
K0017,	0017
K0020,	20
K0100,	0100
K0377,	0377
K7000,	7000

/PAGE 0 ROUTINE POINTERS
KENT,	ENT	/ENTRY/START ADDRESS
KRCVBK,	RCVBLK	/RECEIVE A LINCTAPE BLOCK
KWTBLK,	WRTBLK	/WRITE A LINCTAPE BLOCK
KCHBLK,	CHKBLK	/CHECK WRITTEN BLOCKS

/PAGE 0 ROUTINES
/SEND ONE BYTE OVER SERIAL.
/PARAM[AC]	BYTE TO SEND
/AC IS LEFT UNTOUCHED
SEND,	0
	TLS2		/SEND THE BYTE
	TSF2		/WAIT UNTIL DONE
	JMP .-1
	JMP I SEND	/RETURN

/SEND ONE WORD AS TWO BYTES OVER SERIAL
/PARAM[AC]	WORD TO SEND
/AC WILL BE LEFT EMPTY
SEND2,	0
	JMS SEND	/SEND OFF BOTTOM 8
	RTL;RTL;RAL	/SHIFT TOP 4 INTO BOTTOM 4
	AND K0017	/CUT OFF BOTTOM 4
	JMS SEND	/SEND THEM OFF
	CLA
	JMP I SEND2

/SETUP LINCTAPE FOR A READ OR WRITE TO BUFFER
/THIS WILL SETUP THE TC12 TO:
/1. OPERATE ON FIELD 0
/2. RUN IN EXTENDED ADDRESS MODE
/3. ACCESS LOCATION DEFINED BY BUFADR
/AC WILL BE LEFT EMPTY
LTSTP,	0
	LINC		/SWITCH TO LINC MODE
	TMA		/SET TMA SETUP REG
	1020		/LDA NEXT WORD
	0030		/EXTENDED ADDR BIT
	AXO		/SET XOB
	PDP		/SWITCH BACK TO 8-MODE
	CLA
	JMP I LTSTP	/RETURN

/WAIT FOR TAPE OPERATION TO FINISH
/WILL CAUSE RESET IF SR0 IS SET
/OTHERWISE, RETURNS ON WHEN TAPE DONE FF IS SET
/AC WILL BE LEFT EMPTY
KLWOSR,	CLA OSR	/OSR INSTRUCTION
LTWT,	0
LWSR,	CLA OSR		/GET SWITCH REG
	SPA		/RESET IF SR0 IS SET
	JMP RESET

	RAL		/SHIFT OVER ONE
	CLA SPA		/SKIP IF SR1 SET
	JMP LTWTSK

	TAD K0100	/CHECK IF TAPE DONE FF SET
	TMIR
	JMP LTWT+1
	CLA CLL		/CLEAR LINK TO INDICATE NO-SKIP
	JMP I LTWT
LTWTSK,		/SKIP BLOCK
	TAD K0020	/FORCE I/O PRESET	
	LINC
	ESF
	PDP
LTWTSL,	CLA OSR		/CHECK IF RELEASED
	RAL
	SMA		/LOOP IF NOT
	JMP I LTWT
	JMP LTWTSL

*2000
	KRB2
	JMP .-1

*167	/RESET ENTRY
RESET,	CLA CLL
	TAD RESET	/KILL WAIT SR CHECK
	DCA LWSR
	TAD K0020
	LINC
	ESF		/FORCE IO PRESET
	0707		/SEEK TO BLOCK 0 BY
	0000		/CHECKING IT
	PDP

/ENTRY
*200
ENT,	HLT
	CLA CLL
	TAD KBFADR	/SETUP BUF ADDR FOR SETUP
	JMS LTSTP	/SETUP LINCTAPE

	LINC		/SWITCH TO LINC MODE
	0702		/READ BLOCK 0
	0000
	PDP		/BACK TO 8-MODE
	JMS LTWT	/WAIT FOR READ TO FINSIH
	CLA

	TAD K7000	/READ TMA W/ MAINT INSTRUCTIONS
	TMIR
	CLA
	TMTR
	CIA		/NEGATE
	TAD KBFADR	/ADD BUF ADDR
	CIA		/NEGATE AGAIN
	DCA BLKLEN	/SAVE AS BLOCK LENGTH

	DCA BLKIDX	/CLEAR BLOCK INDEX
	DCA CHKSM	/CLEAR CHECKSUM
	DCA FNSHFG	/CLEAR FINISH FLAG

	TAD KLWOSR	/ENABLE ABORT & SKIP
	DCA LWSR

	TAD BLKLEN	/SEND BLOCK LENGTH
	JMS SEND2

	TAD KBUFSZ	/CALC NUM OF BLKS THAT CAN
	MQL		/FIT IN BUFFER
	TAD BLKLEN
	DCA .+2
	DVI		/BUF SIZE / BLK LEN
	0000
	CLA MQA		/GET QUOTIENT FROM MQ
	DCA BUFCNT

MAINLP,	JMS I KRCVBK	/RECEIVE BLOCK DATA
	JMS I KWTBLK	/WRITE BLOCK DATA TO TAPE
	JMS I KCHBLK	/CHECK WRITTEN BLOCKS

	TAD FNSHFG	/CHECK FINISH FLAG
	CLA SZA
	JMP FINISH	/JUMP TO END

	TAD BLKIDX	/INCREMENT BLOCK NUM/IDX
	TAD BLKCNT	/BY WRITTEN COUNT
	DCA BLKIDX
	JMP MAINLP	/OTHERWISE, LOOP AROUND
FINISH,			/END
	TAD CHKSM	/SEND CHECKSUM
	JMS SEND2

	JMP RESET	/RESET OURSELF

PAGE
/RECEIVE ROUTINES

/RECEIVE SINGLE 8-BIT BYTE OVER SERIAL
/RETURN[AC]	RECEIVED BYTE
RECV,	0
	KSF2		/WAIT UNTIL READY
	JMP .-1
	KRB2		/RECEIVE BYTE
	JMP I RECV	/RETURN

/RECEIVE 12-BIT WORD AS TWO 8-BIT BYTES.
/RETURN[AC]	RECEIVED WORD
RECV2,	0
	JMS RECV	/GET 1ST BYTE
	MQL		/SAVE IN MQ
	JMS RECV	/GET 2ND BYTE
	/AND K0017	/CUT OFF BOTTOM 4
	CLL RTR		/SHIFT INTO TOP 4
	RTR;RAR
	MQA		/OR 1ST INTO BOTTOM 8
	JMP I RECV2	/RETURN

/RECEIVE TWO 12-BITS WORDS AS THREE 8-BIT BYTES
/AC WILL BE EMPTY AFTER THIS RETURNS
/PARAM[RCVBUF]	/RECVEIVE BUFFER ADDR
		/WILL BE INCREMENTED BY 2
		/AFTER CALL
RECV3,	0
			/1ST BYTE WILL BE BOTTOM 4
			/OF 1ST WORD (4 TO 11)
	JMS RECV	/GET 1ST BYTE
	MQL		/SAVE IN MQ
			/2ND BYTE WILL BE TOP 4 OF
			/1ST WORD (0 TO 3) AND BOT
			/4 OF 2ND WORD (8 TO 11)
	JMS RECV	/GET 2ND BYTE
	DCA 1
	TAD 1
	AND K0017	/CUT OFF BOTTOM 4
	CLL RTR		/SHIFT INTO TOP 4
	RTR;RAR
	MQA		/OR 1ST INTO BOTTOM 8
	DCA I RCVBUF	/SAVE TO RECV BUFFER
	ISZ RCVBUF	/INC RECV BUF ADDR
	TAD 1
	CLL RTR		/SHIFT MID 4 INTO BOT 4
	RTR
	AND K0017	/CUT OFF BOTTOM 4
	MQL		/SAVE IN MQ
			/3RD BYTE WILL BE TOP 8
			/OF 2ND WORD
	JMS RECV	/GET 3RD BYTE
	CLL RTL		/SHIFT INTO TOP 8
	RTL
	MQA		/OR BOT 4 BITS FROM 2ND
	DCA I RCVBUF	/SAVE TO RECV BUFFER
	ISZ RCVBUF	/INC RECV BUF ADDR
	JMP I RECV3	/RETURN

/RECEIVE AN ENTIRE LINCTAPE BLOCK OVER SERIAL
/RETURN[KBFADR]	RECEIVED BLOCK DATA
/RETURN[BLKCNT]	NUMBER OF BLOCKS RECEIVED
/RETURN[FNSHFG]	SET IF FINISH FLAG WAS RECEIVED
RCBBCT,	0	/BLK COUNT
RCBEAD,	0	/BLOCK END ADDR
RCVBLK,	0
	TAD BUFCNT	/USE MAX BLOCK COUNT
	CIA
	DCA RCBBCT
	TAD KBFADR	/SETUP RECV BUF ADR
	DCA RCVBUF
RCBBLP,			/REQ BLOCK LOOP
	TAD K0377	/SEND REQUEST FOR A BLOCK
	JMS SEND

	JMS RECV	/RECEIVE STATUS FLAG
	CIA		/CHECK IF == SEND_BLOCK
	TAD K0377
	SZA		/AC>0 IF NOT
	JMP RCBFEN	/JUMP TO END

	TAD BLKLEN	/SETUP END ADDR
	TAD RCVBUF
	CIA
	DCA RCBEAD
RCBWLP,			/RECEIVE BLOCK WORD LOOP
	IAC		/AC=-1 IF AT LAST ODD BLOCK
	SNA		/READ ODD BLOCK IF YES
	JMP RCBOD	/JUMP TO ODD ROUTINE

	JMS RECV3	/RECV TWO WORDS

	TAD RCVBUF	/CHECK IF AT END
	TAD RCBEAD	/AC=0 IF YES
	SZA
	JMP RCBWLP
	JMP RCBWEN	/JUMP TO END
RCBOD,	JMS RECV2	/RECEIVE A SINGLE WORD
	DCA I RCVBUF	/SAVE TO BUFFER
	ISZ RCVBUF	/INC RCV BUFFER
RCBWEN,			/FINISHED RECV BLOCK
	ISZ RCBBCT	/FILLED BUFFER?
	SKP
	JMP RCBBEN	/END IF YES
	JMP RCBBLP	/LOOP BACK AROUND IF NO
RCBFEN,			/FINISH FLAG RECEIVED
	ISZ FNSHFG	/SET FINISH FLAG
RCBBEN,			/RECV'D ALL BLOCKS
	CLA CMA		/PUT BUFADR IN AUTOIDX
	TAD KBFADR
	DCA 10

	TAD RCVBUF	/CALC TOTAL WORDS IN BUF
	CIA
	TAD KBFADR
	DCA RCBEAD
RCBCLP,			/THE FOLLOWING CREATES A
			/CHECKSUM FOR CURRENT BLOCKS
			/THEN ADDS IT TO THE TOTAL SUM
	TAD I 10	/ADD A BLOCK WORD TO CHKSUM
	ISZ RCBEAD	/INC COUNTER
	JMP RCBCLP	/LOOP BACK
	TAD CHKSM	/ADD TO FULL CHECKSUM
	DCA CHKSM	/SAVE CHECKSUM

	TAD RCBBCT	/SAVE NUM OF BLKS IN BUF
	TAD BUFCNT
	DCA BLKCNT
	JMP I RCVBLK	/RETURN

PAGE
/WRITE & CHECK ROUTINES

/PAGE LOCAL VARIABLES
TPOPBO,	0	/BUFFER OFFSET
TPOPCT,	0	/COUNTER

/WRITE BLOCK IMPL
/PARAM[WTBKID]	BLOCK NUMBER TO WRITE
/PARAM[TMA]	TAPE MEM ADDR SETUP WITH WRITE ADDR
/AC WILL BE LEFT EMPTY
WTBKIM,	0
	LINC		/SWITCH TO L-MODE
	0706		/WRI -- WRITE BLOCK
WTBKID,	0000		/BLOCK NUMBER
	PDP		/BACK TO 8-MODE
	JMS LTWT	/WAIT FOR WRITE TO FINISH
	JMP I WTBKIM	/RETURN

/WRITE A BLOCK FROM THE BUFFER TO A TAPE
/PARAM[KBFADR]	BUFFER CONTAINS BLOCK DATA
/PARAM[BLKIDX]	FIRST BLOCK TO BE WRITTEN
/PARAM[BLKCNT]	NUMBER OF BLOCKS TO BE WRITTEN
WRTBLK,	0
	TAD KBFADR	/SETUP WORK BUFF ADDR
	DCA TPOPBO

	TAD BLKIDX	/COPY BLOCK NUMBER TO
	DCA WTBKID	/WRITE BLOCK NUMBER

	TAD BLKCNT	/SETUP COUNTER
	CIA
	DCA TPOPCT
WTBKLP,			/WRITE BLOCK LOOP
	TAD TPOPBO	/SETUP TC12
	JMS LTSTP

	JMS WTBKIM	/ATTEMPT TO WRITE BLOCK
	ISZ WTBKID	/INCREMENT BLOCK NUMBER
	NOP
	ISZ TPOPCT	/INCREMENT COUNTER
	SKP
	JMP I WRTBLK	/RETURN IF ALL WRITTEN

	TAD TPOPBO	/UPDATE BUFF ADDR
	TAD BLKLEN	/TO NEXT BLOCK
	DCA TPOPBO
	JMP WTBKLP	/OTHERWISE, LOOP BACK

/CHECK BLOCKS FOR OBVIOUS CORRUPTION AND RE-WRITE
/IF CORRUPTION IS FOUND
/THIS USES THE LINC 'CHK' INSTRUCTION TO CHECK
/FOR ERROR. THIS IS NOT COMPLETELY RELIABLE
/BUT WILL DETECT MOST ERRORS
/PARAM[KBFADR]	BUFFER CONTAINING BLOCK DATA
/PARAM[BLKIDX]	FIRST BLOCK TO CHECK
/PARAM[BLKCNT]	NUMBER OF BLOCKS TO CHECK
CHBKTR,	0	/TRY COUNTER
CHKBLK,	0
	CLA
	TAD BLKCNT	/SETUP COUNTER
	CIA
	DCA TPOPCT

	TAD KBFADR	/SETUP BUFFER OFFSET
	DCA TPOPBO

	TAD BLKIDX	/COPY BLK NUM TO CHK NUM
	DCA CHBKID
CHBKLP,			/CHECK LOOP
	TAD KTRYCT	/SETUP TRY COUNT
	IAC
	CIA
	DCA CHBKTR
CHBKL2,	JMS LTSTP	/SETUP TC12/LINCTAPE

	LINC		/SWITCH TO L-MODE
	0707		/CHECK BLOCK INST
CHBKID,	0000		/CHECK BLOCK NUM
	PDP		/BACK TO 8-MODE

	JMS LTWT	/WAIT FOR OP TO FINISH

	LINC		/SWITCH TO L-MODE
	TAC		/TO GET TAC
	PDP

	IAC		/CHECK IF ITS 7777
	CLA SZA		/AC=0 IF YES
	JMP CHBKER	/TRY TO HANDLE ERROR

CHBKPE,	TAD TPOPBO	/INC BUFFER OFFSET
	TAD BLKLEN
	DCA TPOPBO

	ISZ CHBKID	/INCREMENT BLOCK NUM
	NOP

	ISZ TPOPCT	/INCREMENT COUNTER & LOOP
	SKP
	JMP I CHKBLK	/RETURN IF DONE
	JMP CHBKLP	/LOOP BACK
CHBKER,			/ERROR HANDLING/CORRECTION
	ISZ CHBKTR	/CHECK IF OUT OF TRIES
	SKP
	JMP CHBKSE	/SEND ERROR IF YES

	TAD CHBKID	/SET WRITE BLK TO CHK BLK
	DCA WTBKID

	TAD TPOPBO	/SETUP TC12
	JMS LTSTP

	JMS WTBKIM	/ATTEMPT TO WRITE
	JMP CHBKL2	/CHECK AGAIN
CHBKSE,			/SEND ERROR OVER SERIAL
	CLA STL RAL	/0XFD = CHKSM BAD
	TAD K0377
	JMS SEND	/SEND CODE

	CLA
	TAD CHBKID	/SEND BAD BLK NUM
	JMS SEND2

	JMP CHBKPE	/CONTINUE CHECKING OTHER BLKS

PAGE

/TAPE READ & WRITE BUFFER
BUF,	ZBLOCK 400
